== Trivia==
*Goblins are small, grotesque, monstrous creatures that appear in the folklore of multiple European cultures. First attested in stories from the Middle Ages, they are ascribed conflicting abilities, temperaments, and appearances depending on the story and country of origin, ranging from mischievous household spirits to malicious, bestial thieves. They often have magical abilities similar to a fairy or demon, such as the ability to shapeshift. Similar creatures include [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duende duendes], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kobold kobolds], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun leprechauns], and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul ghouls].
**In the German and Dutch language setting of the game, the Goblin Giant's name translates to "Kobold Giant". In the Spanish, Arabic, and Vietnamese language setting of the game, the Goblin Giant's name translates to "Duende Giant", "Giant Ghoul", and "Giant Leprechaun" respectively.
**The Goblin Giant is 1 of 6 evolved [[cards]] associated with [[Goblins]], with the others being [[Mortar/Evolution|Mortar]], [[Dart Goblin/Evolution|Dart Goblin]], [[Goblin Cage/Evolution|Goblin Cage]], [[Goblin Barrel/Evolution|Goblin Barrel]], and [[Goblin Drill/Evolution|Goblin Drill]].
*The Goblin Giant's Evolution is 1 of 2 evolved cards to have an alliterative name, the others being the [[Royal Recruits/Evolution|Royal Recruits]].
*Even though the card spawns 2 [[Spear Goblins]], the card image and card render display 3 Spear Goblins.
*The Evolved Goblin Giant is similar to the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Yeti Yeti], a troop from Clash of Clans.
*When the Evolved Goblin Giant's hitpoints drop to activate his Goblin spawns, the sack on his back will glow purple.
*The Goblin Giant's Evolution is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].

